cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "If It Were a Person: Incident, Law, and Precedent Dataset for 1,786 AI Incident Database Incidents"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
authors:
  - family-names: Gilly
    given-names: Travis
    affiliation: Real Safety AI Foundation
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2954-6313"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
url: "https://github.com/princesshobbes/If_It_Were_a_Person_dataset"
repository-code: "https://github.com/princesshobbes/If_It_Were_a_Person_dataset"
abstract: >-
  Every incident in the AI Incident Database through November 2, 2026
  (1,786 incidents), read against one question: if a person had done
  exactly what the record describes, would existing US law treat it as a
  crime, a civil wrong, a breach of a preventive rule, or nothing? Each
  incident is answered under the law in force today and under the law in
  force on the incident date, with the laws cited, how the responsible
  company is reached, and what would change for the company if the AI
  system were treated as a legal person.
keywords:
  - AI incidents
  - AI Incident Database
  - AI liability
  - legal personhood
  - criminal law
  - tort law
  - civil rights
